<section class="page-head">
  <span class="eyebrow">Sylhet Education Board</span>
  <h1>SSC Result 2026 Sylhet Board with Marksheet</h1>
  <p>Everything a Sylhet Board student needs for the SSC Result 2026: the expected date, checking steps, the SMS code, and the board's recent record.</p>
</section>

<nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"></nav>

<main class="wrap-article">
  <article class="doc">
    <p class="updated">Updated 26 July 2026</p>

    <p class="lede">This page covers the <strong>SSC Result 2026 Sylhet Board</strong> for students under the <strong>Sylhet Education Board</strong>: the expected date, how to check your result <strong>with marksheet</strong>, the SMS code, and how Sylhet has performed recently, all specific to this board.</p>

    <div class="keybox">
      <h3>Sylhet Board SSC Result 2026: quick facts</h3>
      <dl>
        <dt>Board</dt><dd>Sylhet Education Board (sylhetboard.gov.bd)</dd>
        <dt>Expected date</dt><dd><b>Last week of July 2026</b> (postponed from 20 July)</dd>
        <dt>Publish time</dt><dd>2:00 PM, with all 11 boards together</dd>
        <dt>SMS code</dt><dd><span class="sms-code">SYL</span></dd>
        <dt>Region</dt><dd>Sylhet division districts</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <h2><span class="n">SECTION 01</span>When Will the Sylhet Board SSC Result 2026 Come Out?</h2>
    <p>The result was first set for <strong>20 July 2026</strong>, then postponed; the boards now expect the <strong>last week of July</strong>, released at <strong>2:00 PM</strong> with every board. A short delay does not change your marks, so rely only on official Sylhet Board notices rather than unofficial dates. We update this page the moment a firm date is confirmed.</p>
    <div class="callout gold"><p><strong>Please note:</strong> the final date is not yet fixed in writing by the Ministry of Education. Treat "last week of July" as a strong expectation and follow the announcement bar on our homepage.</p></div>

    <h2><span class="n">SECTION 02</span>How to Check SSC Result 2026 Sylhet Board Online</h2>
    <p>The online method shows the <strong>full marksheet</strong> with a grade in every subject. Keep your <strong>admit card</strong> (roll) and <strong>registration card</strong> ready.</p>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><strong>Open an official portal.</strong> Use <a href="https://eboardresults.com/v2/home" target="_blank" rel="noopener">eboardresults.com</a>, <a href="https://www.educationboardresults.gov.bd/v2/home" target="_blank" rel="noopener">educationboardresults.gov.bd</a>, or sylhetboard.gov.bd.</li>
      <li><strong>Select SSC/Dakhil/Equivalent.</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Choose the year 2026.</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Select Sylhet</strong> as your board.</li>
      <li><strong>Enter your roll and registration number.</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Answer the security check</strong> and press Get Result.</li>
      <li><strong>Save your marksheet</strong> straight away.</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="callout green"><p><strong>If the site is slow, stay calm.</strong> Heavy traffic at 2:00 PM slows the servers for everyone. Refresh after a moment, or use SMS below, which does not depend on the website.</p></div>

    <h2><span class="n">SECTION 03</span>Check Sylhet Board Result 2026 by SMS</h2>
    <p>SMS works on any handset with no internet. Send this to <strong>16222</strong>:</p>
    <div class="callout green"><p style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--green-deep);margin:0;text-align:center">SSC SYL &lt;ROLL&gt; 2026</p></div>
    <p>Replace <em>&lt;ROLL&gt;</em> with your roll number. For roll 123456 you would send <span class="sms-code">SSC SYL 123456 2026</span> to 16222 and receive your GPA by return message. A small charge applies. Prepare it before 2:00 PM and keep it in drafts.</p>

    <figure class="sms-figure">
      <img src="/assets/ssc-result-sms-format.svg" alt="How to check SSC Result 2026 by SMS: type SSC space SYL space roll number space 2026 and send to 16222" width="800" height="420" loading="lazy">
      <figcaption>SSC Result 2026 SMS format. Send to 16222.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h2><span class="n">SECTION 04</span>Sylhet Board SSC Result 2025: The Numbers</h2>
    <p>Last year is your clearest guide. In <strong>2025</strong>, Sylhet recorded a pass rate of <strong>68.57 percent</strong>. About <strong>1,02,219</strong> students appeared, <strong>70,091</strong> passed, and <strong>3,614</strong> earned GPA 5. Unusually, the split was very close: 1,791 male and 1,823 female GPA 5 holders, and the male pass rate (68.62 percent) edged the female rate (68.54 percent).</p>
    <div class="cards">
      <div class="stat"><div class="big">68.57%</div><div class="lbl">2025 pass rate</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="big">3,614</div><div class="lbl">GPA-5 in 2025</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="big">1.02 L</div><div class="lbl">Appeared</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="big">70,091</div><div class="lbl">Passed</div></div>
    </div>
    <p>Sylhet is the smallest general board by candidate numbers, and its GPA 5 count is correspondingly modest. Interestingly, its 2025 pass rate of 68.57 percent held up better than several larger boards, sitting just above the national average of 68.45 percent.</p>

    <h2><span class="n">SECTION 05</span>Sylhet Board Pass Rate: Recent Trend</h2>
    <p>Sylhet has often sat at the lower end of the boards, so its 2025 figure is close to its recent range.</p>
    <div class="chart">
      <div class="ct">Sylhet Board SSC pass rate, 2022 to 2025 (%)</div>
      <div class="bar"><span class="yr">2022</span><span class="track"><span class="fill" style="width:78.82%"></span></span><span class="val">78.82</span></div>
      <div class="bar"><span class="yr">2023</span><span class="track"><span class="fill" style="width:76.06%"></span></span><span class="val">76.06</span></div>
      <div class="bar"><span class="yr">2024</span><span class="track"><span class="fill" style="width:73.35%"></span></span><span class="val">73.35</span></div>
      <div class="bar"><span class="yr">2025</span><span class="track"><span class="fill low" style="width:68.57%"></span></span><span class="val">68.57</span></div>
      <div class="cap">Sylhet has eased down gradually, from around 78.82% in 2022 to <strong>68.57%</strong> in 2025, a gentler slope than most boards.</div>
    </div>
    <p>What does this mean for you? Because Sylhet's decline has been steadier than the national plunge, a good 2026 result here carries real weight, and it stands out against a board that competes hard for a smaller pool of top college seats across the Sylhet division.</p>

    <h2><span class="n">SECTION 06</span>Sylhet Board Result 2026 with Full Marksheet</h2>
    <p>For the <strong>subject-wise marksheet with number and grade</strong>, use the online method and enter <em>both</em> your roll and registration number, since SMS returns only the GPA. The result page then lists each subject with its grade and grade point, followed by your overall GPA.</p>
    <p>Beyond the headline GPA, the marksheet is worth reading in full. It shows the grade you earned in every subject, which tells you where you were strong and where a subject dragged the average down. That detail matters for the group and college you target next, and it is the same sheet colleges look at during admission, so take a moment to understand every line rather than glancing only at the final number.</p>

    
    <h3>Understanding your GPA on the marksheet</h3>
    <p>The number everyone looks at first is the <strong>GPA</strong>, scored from 1.00 to 5.00, where the top grade of <strong>GPA 5.00</strong> is what students call A+. Each subject carries a letter grade and a matching grade point, and your GPA is the average across them, with the optional <strong>4th subject</strong> adjusted specially: points above a grade C in the 4th subject are added to your total, which is how many students reach a full 5.00. To pass overall you need at least a grade D, meaning grade point 1.00, in every compulsory and elective subject. One F pulls that subject into fail, so read every row, not just the final figure.</p>
    <div class="tw"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Marks</th><th>Grade</th><th>Grade Point</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>80 to 100</td><td>A+</td><td>5.00</td></tr>
        <tr><td>70 to 79</td><td>A</td><td>4.00</td></tr>
        <tr><td>60 to 69</td><td>A minus</td><td>3.50</td></tr>
        <tr><td>50 to 59</td><td>B</td><td>3.00</td></tr>
        <tr><td>40 to 49</td><td>C</td><td>2.00</td></tr>
        <tr><td>33 to 39</td><td>D</td><td>1.00</td></tr>
        <tr><td>0 to 32</td><td>F</td><td>0.00</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>

    <p>The version shown online is the provisional grade sheet; the printed grade sheet and certificate follow through your school, but the online copy is accepted for class XI admission, so you can start applying at once.</p>

    <h2><span class="n">SECTION 07</span>If Your Sylhet Result Looks Wrong</h2>
    <p>Should a subject look lower than you expected, you may apply for <strong>re-scrutiny</strong>, the board challenge. It re-checks the marking mechanics, whether every answer was marked and the marks added and carried correctly, rather than re-marking your script. Applications open the day after results for about a week, are made by SMS from a Teletalk SIM in a format beginning with <span class="sms-code">RSC</span>, and cost roughly 125 to 150 Taka per subject. Apply only for subjects you genuinely doubt, since most applications do not change a grade.</p>

    
    <h3>Common mistakes to avoid on result day</h3>
    <p>A few simple errors trip up Sylhet Board students every year, and all of them are easy to sidestep. First, entering the wrong <strong>registration number</strong>: the roll and registration are different numbers, and the full marksheet will not open without the correct registration, so check your registration card before you start. Second, trusting <strong>unofficial mirror sites</strong> that promise a faster result; they may show wrong data or misuse the roll and registration you type in, so stay on the official portals or a trusted checker. Third, giving up when the site stalls at 2:00 PM; that is congestion, not a missing result, and the SMS route to 16222 sidesteps it entirely. Finally, forgetting to <strong>save</strong> the marksheet once it loads; take a screenshot and use the print option immediately, because you will need it for college admission and the servers may slow again later in the day.</p>

    <h2><span class="n">SECTION 08</span>After the Result: College Admission</h2>
    <p>For most Sylhet Board students, the result quickly becomes a question of <em>which college next?</em> Class XI admission runs through a central online system that opens soon after results, and this year's delay makes the gap tighter than usual. Admission is largely merit based on your SSC GPA and, for many colleges, your group and subject grades. Build a shortlist in three tiers, a few ambitious names such as the leading colleges of Sylhet city, several realistic choices, and a couple of safe options, and be ready to apply the moment the circular appears.</p>

    <h2><span class="n">SECTION 09</span>Summary</h2>
    <p>In short: the <strong>SSC Result 2026 Sylhet Board</strong> is expected in the last week of July 2026 at 2:00 PM. Check online at eboardresults.com with your roll and registration for the marksheet, or text <span class="sms-code">SSC SYL &lt;ROLL&gt; 2026</span> to 16222 for a quick GPA. Sylhet scored 68.57 percent in 2025, just above the national average, with 3,614 GPA 5. Keep your documents ready, save the marksheet immediately, and use re-scrutiny only where justified.</p>

